<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for Avenkin.

  This manifest ships with both phone-only and glasses-beta builds and describes
  optional data routes present in both. Each submission must match the archive and
  the App Store Connect privacy answers.

  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes below cover the required-reason APIs actually used in
  this target's source:
    - UserDefaults (app-only and shared App Group suites) -> CA92.1, 1C8F.1
    - File timestamps (HIPAAComplianceService,
      creationDateKey on the app's own container) -> DDA9.1
    - Disk space (DeviceInfoTool, .systemFreeSize) -> E174.1

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes reflect a source audit of what actually leaves the
  device. Avenkin has no developer-operated backend or user account: every
  transmission is user-directed app functionality sent under the user's own API
  keys to third-party providers (Anthropic / OpenAI / Gemini / Groq / OpenRouter
  / etc. for LLM + vision, ElevenLabs / OpenAI / xAI / Gemini for TTS, Deepgram for diarized
  captions, Deepgram or OpenAI for dictation when the wearer chooses a cloud
  recognizer (off by default), Perplexity / Tavily / Brave /
  SearXNG (user-configured) / DuckDuckGo for search, Apple WeatherKit for weather,
  adsb.fi for flights, RTMP / WebRTC for live streaming). There is no analytics, crash-reporting, or advertising SDK, and no
  cross-app/-developer tracking. Requests are authenticated to provider accounts and
  content may identify the user or other people; there is no guaranteed de-identification
  before transmission. Every type below is conservatively Linked=true, Tracking=false,
  purpose = App Functionality. The lack of a first-party account does not establish
  that data is unlinked by third-party recipients.

  Notes for whoever finalizes submission:
    - Health & Fitness data (HealthKit, via FitnessCoachingTool) is surfaced into
      LLM tool results, i.e. transmitted to a third party. Apple forbids using
      HealthKit data for advertising/data-mining and requires user consent for
      third-party sharing — keep purpose strictly AppFunctionality and ensure the
      in-app consent copy covers LLM transmission.
    - Contacts (ContactsTool returns name/phone/email) and Precise Location
      (weather/flight/maps tools) likewise enter LLM context.
    - Apple Music catalogue search (MusicKit, music_control) sends the song /
      artist / album / playlist / station name the wearer asked for to Apple.
      No SDK is linked for it (MusicKit is a system framework; the developer
      token comes from the App ID's MusicKit App Service). Declared under
      SearchHistory, AppFunctionality, linked, not tracking.
    - Weather comes from Apple's WeatherKit (get_weather, My Day). No SDK is
      linked for it (WeatherKit is a system framework, authorised by the
      com.apple.developer.weatherkit entitlement and the App ID's WeatherKit App
      Service). Coordinates rounded to ~1 km, or a named place geocoded on the
      phone, are sent to Apple. Declared under PreciseLocation, AppFunctionality,
      linked, not tracking. Blocked under Medical Local Only.
    - A job handover to an expert (Field Assist, escalate_to_expert 'send' or the
      job's "Send the job to an expert") sends the job's details, the photos the
      technician picks with faces blurred, and the conversation where allowed, to
      an expert the technician chooses, by the technician's own Messages, Mail or
      share sheet. No new service or network route: the file goes the way any
      attachment goes, and only on the technician's tap. Never in Medical
      Compliance mode.
    - A job handover opened on an expert's phone (Assisting) is kept on that
      phone only, apart from everything else, for the days the sending
      organisation set after Done, then deleted; it never reaches the assistant,
      its memory, search or team learnings. The expert's time reply (minutes,
      the updates seen, a note and their expert card's details) goes back only
      by the expert's own share sheet. No new service or network route; not a
      data collection by the developer.
    - Keep these declarations aligned with App Store Connect and verified provider
      retention/use terms. Arbitrary user-configured recipients do not establish a
      blanket guarantee about third-party data handling.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<!-- Voice/transcripts to LLMs, mic audio to Gemini Live / OpenAI Realtime, text to ElevenLabs / OpenAI / xAI / Gemini TTS,
	     diarized-caption audio to Deepgram, and the audio of each question to Deepgram or OpenAI when the
	     wearer chooses cloud dictation (off by default; never in HIPAA mode) -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeAudioData</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- Glasses camera frames sent to LLM vision; live video via RTMP / WebRTC -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePhotosorVideos</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- Prompts, notes, meeting summaries, message drafts sent to LLM providers -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUserContent</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- lat/lon sent to weather (Apple WeatherKit, rounded to ~1 km), flights (adsb.fi), maps, and into LLM context -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePreciseLocation</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- WeatherKit uses coordinates rounded to approximately one kilometre. -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeCoarseLocation</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array><string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string></array>
        </dict>
		<!-- HealthKit reads (FitnessCoachingTool) surfaced into LLM tool results -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeHealth</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeFitness</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- ContactsTool returns name/phone/email of looked-up contacts to the LLM -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeContacts</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<!-- Web search queries sent to Perplexity / Tavily / Brave / SearXNG (user-configured) / DuckDuckGo;
		     music names the wearer asks to play or add, sent to Apple's catalogue through MusicKit
		     (subscribers only; library-only under Medical Local Only) -->
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeSearchHistory</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>DDA9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>E174.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
